' plan-114-D: a record carrying a resource is NOT comparable.
'
' This needed no new code -- it is proven, not built. `is_comparable_seen`'s
' record arm maps every field through `resource_base_type`, which strips the
' `RES ` marker, and `is_resource_name` then answers false for the resource
' underneath. So the record was already non-comparable the moment a `RES` field
' became expressible.
'
' A fixture rather than a claim, because "it already works" is exactly the kind
' of assertion that is true when written and false two refactors later. If
' someone makes a resource comparable, or makes the record arm stop stripping
' the marker, this fixture is what says so.
IMPORT fs
IMPORT io

TYPE Holder
  handle AS RES fs::File
END TYPE

FUNC main AS Integer
  RES a AS fs::File = fs::openFile("target/cmp-a.txt", "w")
  RES b AS fs::File = fs::openFile("target/cmp-b.txt", "w")
  LET x = Holder[a]
  LET y = Holder[b]
  IF x = y THEN
    io::print("unreachable")
  END IF
  RETURN 0
END FUNC
